Embedded LKM integrity pin (gate present in master from PR #3)
---------------------------------------------------------------

The fail-closed KO SHA-256 gate and the final packaged-byte verification
summarized in "Validation status and release gates" above are **present in
master from PR #3** (merged into master at `cdec576`) and are enforced by a
build from this checkout. At the earlier historical base (`9f60e16`) the KO
was only an input dependency of `app/src/main/jni/CMakeLists.txt`, with no
verification target; that snapshot is retained below only as a historical
record.

`app/src/main/jni/verify_ko_sha256.cmake` checks the SHA-256 of the
gitignored, build-supplied `app/src/main/jni/ko/dfroot-android13-5.15.ko` at
build time, before the blob is embedded into `exp.c`. The two reported
fingerprints below are **repository records from that earlier snapshot, not
verified output of the current build or a recorded source/build-input
identity**:

  - 94f8be987a2f8bdc13539e42a5c3cb4c0f606024b8b31601496c5d5e5c0025a7
        local `make` output from `lkm/`, 13504 B, WITH `.note.gnu.build-id`.
  - 9dfb8b71b306f5a38fd8b35b283d4dab8b4eb25a08ad97ca0f4ef705b6151c68
        CI artifact, 13384 B, post-processed after the DDK build with
        `llvm-objcopy --strip-unneeded` plus several `-R …` section removals
        (including `.note.gnu.build-id`; see `build.yml`); reported as the KO
        shipped in the v4.8-gzif release APK.

A later #5 CI rebuild was shown to change the bytes: a reviewed re-pin adds
CI-stripped pin `e10425d055ff6803856cc24f6f4fe2e2e09746df195c50503811356eb87df605`
(13,456 B) to `KO_EXPECTED_SHA256S`; the pins above remain historical records.

Any other blob is rejected by the gate (fail-closed); an unknown or tampered
module cannot satisfy the check. At the historical input-only snapshot
`DFROOT_SKIP_KO_HASH_CHECK=ON` disabled that check for local experiments; in
the current master gate the source-only skip option is deprecated/unsupported
and the final linked/packaged bytes are verified mandatorily. Skip mode is
forbidden in CI/release builds, and PR-level CI skips the real publishing
gates and is not distributable-artifact validation. Re-verify for **every**
source/build-input change, and re-pin **only the bytes actually shown to
change** in `app/src/main/jni/CMakeLists.txt` in a reviewed commit before a new
artifact is usable; do not assume every edit changes the blob. A pinned hash
proves equality to an approved blob, not that the blob was built from the
current checkout; the historical source revision and build inputs are not
established by these pins and should be marked unknown. A mutable local
image tag is not equivalent to the CI digest pin.

